  "split_decision": "Copy only the entire independent optional natural data or whole endomap/fixed-predicate component. Preserve mixed own-provider schemas and genuine property proofs in exact archives rather than narrow records, add missing laws or create a legacy self-provider import.",
  "review_notes": [
    "Retain the complete original ChromaticHeight structure: height : Nat, positive? : Option (PLift (0 < height)) and label : String. Its optional dependent proof may be none; height is not universally positive and no chromatic-height construction is provided.",
    "The independent HeightRankRule has an actual function ChromaticHeight -> TensorRank and an independently chosen monotone proposition/proof. Neither order nor a monotonicity equation for that function is stated. Its genuine projection proof remains byte-exact in the archive.",
    "The captured TensorRank is a Nat annotation. No dimension, tensor-rank law, chromatic theory or graph-coloring interpretation follows. The historical organized GraphTheory label remains archive metadata only.",
    "The pure optional dependent-proof data record is a genuine seam independent of the mixed rank-rule record. Copy the entire record, original import/documentation and every field unchanged; no narrowed record, new legacy self-provider import or renamed mathematical field is generated."
  ],
